    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-28T12:00:37+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-28T12:00:37+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-28T01:30:37Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-28T01:30:37Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system south of WA extends a ridge over southern parts of the state while a weak trough lies across central Australia near the norther border. The high will drift over the southeast on Thursday and into the Tasman Sea on Friday, allowing a trough and low pressure system to move across SA on Friday. A brief high pressure system settles over SA on Saturday before another trough and low starts to move across from WA on Sunday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-28T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-29T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-27T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-28T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers north of Marla, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds east to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Daytime maximum temperatures 23 to 29.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">Moderate</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 5:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-29T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-28T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. High chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, slight chance elsewhere. A thunderstorm likely, possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding west of Coober Pedy. Winds east to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h turning northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 12 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-30T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-29T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers east of Coober Pedy, medium chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the morning and afternoon. Winds north to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h shifting west to southwesterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to around 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 27 to 34.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-31T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-01T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-30T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-31T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending southeast to southwesterly during the afternoon then tending northeast to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 29 to 34.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
